usage: order_book_cli replay <file.csv> [--trades] [--events] [--book] [--validate none|final|per-command]
       order_book_cli demo
       order_book_cli --help

Replays a CSV command file (docs/replay-format.md) on an empty order book and prints
replay statistics. Never prompts: everything is set on the command line.

commands:
  replay <file.csv>  replay the file, then print its statistics
  demo               print the events of a short scripted session
  help               print this help

replay options, in any order before or after the file:
  --trades           print each trade, tagged with its command's line, before the statistics
  --events           print every event (acceptances, rejections, trades, and cancels)
                     instead; this includes the trades
  --book             print the final book after the statistics, best price first
  --validate MODE    check the book's invariants: none, final (the default), or
                     per-command (after every command; slower)
  --                 treat the next argument as the file, even if it starts with '-'
  -h, --help         print this help and exit

exit status:
  0  replayed to the end, even if the book rejected some commands; or help printed
  1  input error: the file can't be opened or read, or is malformed (what ran before
     the error is still printed)
  2  usage error
  3  engine failure: the book threw, or failed an invariant check

examples:
  order_book_cli replay orders.csv
  order_book_cli replay orders.csv --trades
  order_book_cli replay orders.csv --trades --book
  order_book_cli replay orders.csv --events --book --validate per-command
